@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Polityka prywatności";
}

<div class="row justify-content-center">
    <article class="col-lg-10 col-xl-9" aria-labelledby="privacy-heading">
        <header class="mb-4">
            <p class="eyebrow">RP-bit / PRIVACY AND PERSONAL DATA</p>
            <h1 id="privacy-heading">Privacy policy</h1>
            <p class="text-muted">Version dated <time datetime="2026-10-31">31 October 2026</time></p>
            <p>This policy explains how personal data is processed in the RP-bit service store.
                Linked external websites may have separate privacy policies.</p>
        </header>

        <section aria-labelledby="administrator-heading">
            <h2 id="administrator-heading" class="h4 mt-5 mb-3">1. Controller and contact</h2>
            <p>RP-bit is the controller of personal data processed through this service.</p>
            <dl>
                <dt>Business</dt>
                <dd>RP-bit</dd>
                <dt>Tax identification number</dt>
                <dd>PL9671255358</dd>
                <dt>Personal data enquiries</dt>
                <dd><a asp-controller="Contact" asp-action="Index">Contact form</a> or
                    <a href="mailto:contact@rp-bit.com">contact@rp-bit.com</a></dd>
            </dl>
            <p>Contact RP-bit directly about data protection and the exercise of your rights.</p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="data-heading">
            <h2 id="data-heading" class="h4 mt-5 mb-3">2. Data we process</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Account:</strong> email address, username, password hash, confirmation
                    status and authentication/security settings. Passwords are not stored as plaintext.</li>
                <li><strong>Profile:</strong> optional phone number, recipient, shipping address,
                    billing name, tax number and billing address. These fields are not required
                    to browse the catalogue or create an account.</li>
                <li><strong>Basket:</strong> selected service identifiers, names, prices, quantities
                    and a session identifier. A basket does not require sign-in and does not create an order.</li>
                <li><strong>Correspondence:</strong> name or company, reply email, topic, message
                    and other information you provide. The form accepts no attachments; later email correspondence may.</li>
                <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> depending on hosting/proxy configuration,
                    logs may include IP addresses, timestamps, requested resources, browser information
                    and errors. The IP address visible to the application is also used for in-memory contact rate limiting.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Do not send passwords, API keys, special-category data or confidential production
                materials through this form or ordinary email. Agree on a suitable transfer method separately.</p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="purposes-heading">
            <h2 id="purposes-heading" class="h4 mt-5 mb-3">3. Purposes and legal bases</h2>
            <p>Under Article 6(1) of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR):</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Account and profile:</strong> performance of the account agreement,
                    Article 6(1)(b). Creating an account is not marketing consent.</li>
                <li><strong>Enquiries and quotations:</strong> steps at your request before a contract,
                    Article 6(1)(b). Business-representative or other correspondence may rely on the
                    legitimate interest in communication, Article 6(1)(f).</li>
                <li><strong>Separately agreed services:</strong> contract performance, Article 6(1)(b).
                    Parties' roles, access and any required processing agreement are agreed before work starts.</li>
                <li><strong>Tax and accounting duties:</strong> legal obligations, Article 6(1)(c), where applicable.</li>
                <li><strong>Security, abuse prevention and legal claims:</strong> legitimate interests,
                    Article 6(1)(f), taking your rights and reasonable expectations into account.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Email and password are needed for an account; contact details are needed for a reply.
                Provide other data only where necessary. Billing details may be required when a service is invoiced.</p>
            <p>The application currently has no newsletter, comments, waiting list, online payments
                or automatic invoicing. A basket or saved billing details do not constitute a contract, payment or invoice.</p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="inquiry-heading">
            <h2 id="inquiry-heading" class="h4 mt-5 mb-3">4. Contact form and enquiries</h2>
            <p>Enquiries from the basket include a pre-filled list and estimated total; a service-page
                enquiry includes its name and indicative price. You may edit the message.
                Profile details are not automatically attached.</p>
            <p>The form sends data through the configured SMTP server to the controller's inbox.
                Your email is used as Reply-To, not as the sender. No automatic copy is sent to you.
                Messages are not saved in the store's database, but may be retained in mail systems and backups.
                An enquiry is not marketing registration.</p>
            <p>Email is handled through Google Workspace. Account confirmation, email-address
                changes and password-reset messages go to the user concerned. These messages
                support account operation and security, not marketing.</p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="recipients-heading">
            <h2 id="recipients-heading" class="h4 mt-5 mb-3">5. Recipients and providers</h2>
            <p>Authorised persons and providers may access data only as needed. Required processing
                arrangements must be in place where a provider acts as a processor.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Mikrus: application and database hosting:</strong> server provision,
                    storage of account/profile data and technical infrastructure operation.
                    The hosting provider may access data as necessary to support the server.</li>
                <li><strong>Cloudflare: DNS, HTTPS, Cloudflare Tunnel and traffic protection:</strong>
                    handling connections, including IP addresses, headers and data in requests
                    and responses. Cloudflare also handles traffic to forms and account pages.</li>
                <li><strong>Google: Google Workspace and Google Fonts:</strong> email,
                    account-related messages, correspondence and the fonts described below.
                    Mail systems process sender/recipient addresses, message content and metadata.</li>
                <li><strong>Persons authorised by RP-bit:</strong> account, correspondence
                    and backup administration, only as needed for their duties.</li>
                <li><strong>Accounting/legal support, if used:</strong> accountants, accounting
                    firms and legal advisers for service billing, legal obligations and claims.</li>
                <li>Public authorities: only as required or permitted by law.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>We do not sell users' personal data.</p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="external-heading">
            <h2 id="external-heading" class="h4 mt-5 mb-3">6. External resources and international transfers</h2>
            <p>The logo and service images are hosted with the application. Manrope is loaded from
                Google Fonts at <code>fonts.googleapis.com</code> and <code>fonts.gstatic.com</code>.
                These requests may disclose your IP address, browser information and referring website
                to Google. They are not an integration with Google Analytics or advertising consent.</p>
            <p>Provider information:
                <a href="https://developers.google.com/fonts/faq/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Fonts privacy FAQ</a>
                and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google privacy policy</a>.
                These links do not replace the controller's assessment.</p>
            <p>Google and Cloudflare use international infrastructure. Data may be processed outside
                the European Economic Area, including in the United States. This service does not
                guarantee that all data stays in Poland or the EEA. For transfers covered by their
                processing agreements, providers include European Commission-approved standard
                contractual clauses and, where applicable, adequacy decisions including the EU-US
                Data Privacy Framework.</p>
            <p>Safeguards and subprocessors are described in the
                <a href="https://cloud.google.com/terms/data-processing-addendum/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Workspace data processing terms</a>
                and <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-customer-dpa/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare data processing addendum</a>.
                Google Fonts requests are subject to the Google privacy information linked above,
                not automatically to the Google Workspace agreement. Contact RP-bit for information
                about transfers affecting your data and a copy of the relevant safeguards,
                subject to the protection of confidential information.</p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="retention-heading">
            <h2 id="retention-heading" class="h4 mt-5 mb-3">7. Retention</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Account/profile: for the account's lifetime. Deletion does not automatically erase
                    correspondence or records retained on another legal basis.</li>
                <li>Basket: session data expires after 30 minutes of inactivity; in-memory data may also be lost on restart.</li>
                <li>Uncontracted enquiries: until the matter is closed, then no longer than 12 months
                    from the last contact where correspondence is needed for further discussions.
                    Messages relating to a contract, legal obligation or claim follow the relevant
                    retention period below.</li>
                <li>Service records/claims: for performance and the applicable limitation or mandatory retention period.</li>
                <li>Tax records: generally five years from the end of the calendar year in which the
                    payment deadline expired, subject to specific rules and suspension/interruption.
                    This is not automatically five years from the invoice date.</li>
                <li>Service technical logs: until the oldest entries are removed through size-limited
                    rotation. The production container configuration limits each service to three
                    10 MiB files; elapsed retention depends on traffic and events. Records preserved
                    for an incident may be kept until it is resolved and, if necessary, for the
                    applicable period for establishing, exercising or defending claims.</li>
                <li>Recovery backups maintained by RP-bit: no longer than 28 days from creation.
                    Data deleted from the active database may remain in older backups until retired
                    within this cycle. Backups are used only for disaster recovery; after restoration,
                    previously fulfilled erasure requests are applied again.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Data must not be retained indefinitely just in case. When the purpose or legal basis
                ends, delete or effectively anonymise it, subject to legal duties and backup rules.</p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="rights-heading">
            <h2 id="rights-heading" class="h4 mt-5 mb-3">8. Your rights</h2>
            <p>Subject to the GDPR's conditions and limits, you may request access/a copy, rectification,
                erasure, restriction and portability for eligible automated processing based on consent
                or contract. You may object to legitimate-interest processing on grounds relating to
                your situation, and unconditionally to direct marketing if it is introduced. Where
                processing relies on consent, you may withdraw it without affecting earlier lawful processing.</p>
            <p>Edit your profile in <a asp-area="Identity" asp-page="/Account/Manage/Index">account settings</a>.
                Signed-in users can download their data or delete their account under
                <a asp-area="Identity" asp-page="/Account/Manage/PersonalData">personal data</a>.
                These tools do not replace requests concerning other data, such as correspondence.</p>
            <p>Use the <a asp-controller="Contact" asp-action="Index">contact form</a> or
                <a href="mailto:contact@rp-bit.com">contact@rp-bit.com</a>. Where reasonably necessary
                we may request proportionate identity verification. We respond without undue delay,
                generally within one month. Complex or numerous requests may require two further months;
                we explain the extension within the first month.</p>
            <p>Erasure is not absolute. Any refusal or limitation requires a legal basis, such as
                mandatory retention or establishing, exercising or defending legal claims.</p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="cookies-heading">
            <h2 id="cookies-heading" class="h4 mt-5 mb-3">9. Cookies</h2>
            <p>Technical cookies support authentication, basket sessions, CSRF protection, language
                preference and short-lived status messages. The basket is stored server-side;
                its cookie contains a session identifier.</p>
            <div class="table-responsive">
                <table class="table">
                    <caption class="text-muted">Standard ASP.NET Core cookies; some names have variable suffixes.</caption>
                    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Cookie</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th><th scope="col">Lifetime</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td><code>__Host-RpBit.Auth</code></td><td>Signed-in session.</td><td>Browser session, or up to 8 hours with persistent sign-in. Authentication expires within 8 hours without automatic renewal.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>__Host-RpBit.Session</code></td><td>Server-side basket association.</td><td>Session cookie; basket data expires after 30 minutes of inactivity independently.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>__Host-RpBit.Antiforgery</code></td><td>Cross-site request protection.</td><td>Usually the browser session.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>.AspNetCore.Culture</code></td><td>PL/EN preference.</td><td>Up to one year after the last language change or until deleted.</td></tr>
                        <tr><td><code>.AspNetCore.Mvc.CookieTempDataProvider</code></td><td>Short-lived operation messages.</td><td>Until read or session end, depending on usage.</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <p>Strictly necessary cookies for a requested service generally do not require optional-cookie
                consent. Visiting, scrolling or closing a notice is not advertising/analytics consent.</p>
            <p>The application currently has no Google Analytics, Google Ads or Meta Pixel. Any future
                optional analytics/advertising requires a legal assessment, updated information and,
                where required, prior consent and a way to withdraw it before those mechanisms operate.</p>
            <p>Manage cookies in your browser. Blocking technical cookies may prevent sign-in, form
                submission or basket persistence. Deleting cookies does not delete your account or stored data.</p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="security-heading">
            <h2 id="security-heading" class="h4 mt-5 mb-3">10. Security and automated decisions</h2>
            <p>The application uses authentication, access control, password hashing and CSRF protection.
                Infrastructure and administrative access controls must match the actual deployment.
                No system guarantees elimination of all risk.</p>
            <p>The current application makes no solely automated decisions producing legal or similarly
                significant effects, and performs no advertising profiling. Listing AI services does
                not automatically transfer account data to AI models.</p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="complaints-heading">
            <h2 id="complaints-heading" class="h4 mt-5 mb-3">11. Complaints and changes</h2>
            <p>You may complain to the President of the Polish Personal Data Protection Office
                (UODO) if you believe processing infringes data protection law. Current details are on
                <a href="https://uodo.gov.pl/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the official UODO website</a>.
                Contacting us first is optional, not a prerequisite for a complaint.</p>
            <p>This policy must be updated when processing purposes, features, providers, technology
                or law changes. The current version and date appear here. Publishing an update does
                not replace any required notification or new consent.</p>
        </section>
    </article>
</div>